{%- comment -%}
  Badge — 5 variants.

  Styles: ../component-library/css/components.css (.badge and modifiers)

  Variants (the `type` argument):
    sale         -> .badge--sale        Cameleer fill, heading label
    in-stock     -> .badge--stock       darkened Dusty Canyon, white label
    authentic    -> .badge--authentic   Cultural Accent date red  ⚠ ORIGINALS ONLY
    new          -> .badge--new         card fill, hairline border
    best-seller  -> .badge--bestseller  gold border, heading label

  ⚠ TWO-REGISTER FIREWALL
  `authentic` is the only badge that draws on the Cultural Accent Set.
  It must never render on an inspired-by product. This snippet enforces
  that itself rather than trusting the caller: pass `product` and an
  authentic badge on a non-Original silently downgrades to `new`.
  Source: Planning/BENCHMARK.md Part 2 §5.

  Accepts:
    text     {String}   visible label. From a setting or a locale key.
                        Falls back to the locale string for `type`.
    type     {String}   sale | in-stock | authentic | new | best-seller
    show_icon {Boolean} prepend the glyph matching `type`
    product  {Product}  optional. Enables the firewall check.
    class    {String}

  Usage:
    {% render 'badge', type: 'in-stock', show_icon: true %}
    {% render 'badge', type: 'authentic', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign badge_type = type | default: 'new'

  comment
    Firewall. An Original is identified by vendor, matching the rule the
    component library already applies. When the vendor field migrates to
    an `inspired_by` metafield (PROJECT-CONTEXT.md §7.4 — still open),
    this is the single place that changes.
  endcomment
  if badge_type == 'authentic' and product != blank
    assign is_original = false
    assign vendor_handle = product.vendor | handle
    if vendor_handle == 'siwa-fragrances' or vendor_handle == 'siwa-original-creation'
      assign is_original = true
    endif
    unless is_original
      assign badge_type = 'new'
    endunless
  endif

  case badge_type
    when 'sale'
      assign modifier = 'badge--sale'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.sale' | t
      assign glyph = ''
    when 'in-stock'
      assign modifier = 'badge--stock'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.in_stock' | t
      assign glyph = 'check'
    when 'sold-out'
      assign modifier = 'badge--soldout'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.sold_out' | t
      assign glyph = ''
    when 'authentic'
      assign modifier = 'badge--authentic'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.authentic' | t
      assign glyph = ''
    when 'best-seller'
      assign modifier = 'badge--bestseller'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.best_seller' | t
      assign glyph = 'star'
    else
      assign modifier = 'badge--new'
      assign fallback = 'products.badges.new' | t
      assign glyph = ''
  endcase

  assign badge_text = text | default: fallback
-%}
{%- if badge_text != blank -%}
  <span class="badge {{ modifier }} {{ class }}">
    {%- if show_icon and glyph != blank -%}
      {%- render 'icon', name: glyph, class: 'badge__icon' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{ badge_text }}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
